ta-text=\"Γρηγώριος\">Γρηγώριος\u003C/span> υἱὸς \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Πο\n                    \">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"patronym\" data-text=\"Πο\n                    \">\u003Cspan data-text=\"Πο\">Πο\u003C/span>-\u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span> του π\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ρ\u003C/span>(εσ)\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">β\u003C/span>(υτέρου) ζήσας ἔτη κβ´ \u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>[τ(ελ)]ευτᾷ δὲ ἐν \u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">Κ\u003C/span>(υρί)\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ῳ\u003C/span> μηνὴ Ἰ\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ου\u003C/span>(λίῳ) \u003Cbr id=\"al5-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>ἰν\u003Cspan class=\"intraline\" title=\"line through\">δ\u003C/span>(ικτιῶνος) η´ \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"author":3,"date":4,"citedRange":112,"ptr":113,"ref":115,"inscriptionDate":4,"title":2,"citation":5,"uri":6,"year":4},"92 n.20",{"target":114},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/6KPB9V5B",{"_":116,"target":116},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001787",2006,{"file":119,"uri":119,"title":120,"status":121,"editions":123,"editionAuthor":26,"type":130,"objectType":131,"material":132,"condition":81,"layoutDesc":140,"handNote":144,"date":225,"places":230,"geo":238,"country":71,"provenance":232,"provenanceGeo":242,"region":75,"settlement":232,"repository":245,"idno":249,"textLang":252,"tmNumber":125,"facsimile":254,"letterHeights":261,"publications":299,"zotero":302,"keywords":305,"html":313,"bibl":314,"bulletinDateSort":117,"citedRangeSort":317,"languageSort":83,"materialSort":133,"typeSort":28},"ISic003337","Funerary inscription for Eirena",{"_":122},"edited",[124,126,127,128,129],{"_":125,"type":16},"645584",{"type":18},{"type":20},{"type":22},{"type":25},{"_":28,"ana":29,"ref":30},{"_":32,"ana":33,"ref":34},{"_":133,"ana":134,"type":135,"subtype":136,"resp":139,"ref":41},"Very fine-grained, veined, white marble, likely Pavonazzetto, Docimian. Digital microscopy: indistinguishable fabric. Scribbly veins, maybe a limestone (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy)","#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Pavonazzetto #material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Docimian","stone.marble",[137,138],"Pavonazzetto","Docimian","#Coccato",{"layout":141},{"p":142,"rs":143,"damage":81},"Ten lines of Greek filling the available space, decreasing notably in size in the second five lines",{"_":48,"ana":49,"ref":50},{"lettering":145,"dimensions":146},"The letters are engraved in a fairly plain, square fashion, with simple serifs. Alpha is mostly with broken bar, sometimes with an extended upper serif, although there is a straight bar example in line 7 and in lines 8 and 10 straight bar descending to left foot; beta is closed, with larger lower eye, generally horizontal along the base; delta varies between regular triangle and oblique lower bar with extended serif above; epsilon has straight bars of equal length, except for instances in lines 9 and 10 when it is lunate; theta is ovoid with connecting straight bar; kappa has short tails; lambda sometimes has an extended upper serif; mu varies between a form with vertical first and last hastae and short middle strokes meeting above the line and cursive form comparable to a lower-case mu in line 9; omicron is full size in the first few lines, but increasingly is smaller and mid-line; sigma is consistently lunate, but more often formed of three straight strokes; less often a single curved stroke; omega is consistently lunate, and sometimes smaller and mid-line. The eta and nu are in ligature in lines 5, 6 and 7. In line 5 the omicron in the final word is inscribed above the other letters (due to omission?). The last two/three words of the last line are enclosed between a pair of christograms. Small hedera occur in lines 1, 3, 5, and 10.",[147,151,156,161,166,169,175,180,185,190,196,199,203,206,210,214,216,220,223],{"type":57,"l":58,"from":59,"to":59,"h":148,"unit":60,"atLeast":149,"atMost":150},"12-18","12","18",{"type":57,"l":152,"from":64,"to":64,"h":153,"unit":60,"atLeast":154,"atMost":155},"Line 2","14-19","14","19",{"type":57,"l":157,"from":158,"to":158,"h":159,"unit":60,"atLeast":149,"atMost":160},"Line 3","line3","12-22","22",{"type":57,"l":162,"from":163,"to":163,"h":164,"unit":60,"atLeast":165,"atMost":160},"Line 4","line4","8-22","8",{"type":57,"l":167,"from":168,"to":168,"h":148,"unit":60,"atLeast":149,"atMost":150},"Line 5","line5",{"type":57,"l":170,"from":171,"to":171,"h":172,"unit":60,"atLeast":173,"atMost":174},"Line 6","line6","9-16","9","16",{"type":57,"l":176,"from":177,"to":177,"h":178,"unit":60,"atLeast":179,"atMost":154},"Line 7","line7","7-14","7",{"type":57,"l":181,"from":182,"to":182,"h":183,"unit":60,"atLeast":184,"atMost":149},"Line 8","line8","6-12","6",{"type":57,"l":186,"from":187,"to":187,"h":188,"unit":60,"atLeast":184,"atMost":189},"Line 9","line9","6-10","10",{"type":57,"l":191,"from":192,"to":192,"h":193,"unit":60,"atLeast":194,"atMost":195},"Line 10","line10","5-13","5","13",{"type":62,"l":63,"from":59,"to":64,"h":197,"unit":60,"atLeast":189,"atMost":198},"10-15","15",{"type":62,"l":200,"from":64,"to":158,"h":201,"unit":60,"atLeast":202,"atMost":179},"Interlineation line 2 to 3","3-7","3",{"type":62,"l":204,"from":158,"to":163,"h":205,"unit":60,"atLeast":194,"atMost":198},"Interlineation line 3 to 4","5-15",{"type":62,"l":207,"from":163,"to":168,"h":208,"unit":60,"atLeast":209,"atMost":189},"Interlineation line 4 to 5","4-10","4",{"type":62,"l":211,"from":168,"to":171,"h":212,"unit":60,"atLeast":213,"atMost":179},"Interlineation line 5 to 6","2-7","2",{"type":62,"l":215,"from":171,"to":177,"h":212,"unit":60,"atLeast":213,"atMost":179},"Interlineation line 6 to 7",{"type":62,"l":217,"from":177,"to":182,"h":218,"unit":60,"atLeast":219,"atMost":184},"Interlineation line 7 to 8","1-6","1",{"type":62,"l":221,"from":182,"to":187,"h":222,"unit":60,"atLeast":219,"atMost":194},"Interlineation line 8 to 9","1-5",{"type":62,"l":224,"from":187,"to":192,"h":222,"unit":60,"atLeast":219,"atMost":194},"Interlineation line 9 to 10",{"_":226,"notBefore":227,"notAfter":228,"evidence":229},"5th century CE, with a likely terminus post quem of 403-408 CE, given that a coin of that date was found within the tomb (Tigano 2009: 164; more generally, the tombs of this part of the necropolis all date late 4th to 5th century CE)",403,500,"archaeological-context",[231,234],{"_":232,"type":72,"ref":233,"region":71},"Halaesa","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462225",{"_":235,"type":76,"ref":236,"offset":237,"region":71},"Castel di Tusa","http://sws.geonames.org/2525099","near",[239],[240,241],37.99907,14.26197,[243,244],38.0073241,14.2527381,{"_":246,"role":247,"ref":248},"Antiquarium e sito archeologico di Halaesa ","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/053",{"_":250,"type":251},"ME 20272","inventory",{"_":83,"mainLang":84,"languages":253},[83],{"n":255,"url":256,"height":257,"width":258,"desc":259,"surfaceType":260},"screen","ISic003337_tiled.tif","3387px","5310px","Photo J. Prag courtesy Soprintendenza BBCCAA di Messina","front",[262,265,268,270,272,273,276,278,280,282,285,287,289,290,292,294,295,297,298],{"atLeast":263,"atMost":264},12,18,{"atLeast":266,"atMost":267},14,19,{"atLeast":263,"atMost":269},22,{"atLeast":271,"atMost":269},8,{"atLeast":263,"atMost":264},{"atLeast":274,"atMost":275},9,16,{"atLeast":277,"atMost":266},7,{"atLeast":279,"atMost":263},6,{"atLeast":279,"atMost":281},10,{"atLeast":283,"atMost":284},5,13,{"atLeast":281,"atMost":286},15,{"atLeast":288,"atMost":277},3,{"atLeast":283,